<title>USA: Delaware Gov to sign bills for $354 mln in bonds.</title>
<headline>Delaware Gov to sign bills for $354 mln in bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delaware Gov. Thomas Carper said Tuesday he planned to sign the state's $354 million 1998 capital spending plan into law at a ceremony Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bill calls for $125.2 million for transportation and road improvements; $179.9 million for schools, prisons, crime, welfare, and job creation; and $49.3 million in aid to local governments and other investments.</p>
<p>The signing ceremony will be held in Wilmington, according to the governor's office.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
